From 0a7d3e206c5e2eb9ea307065a8f406893ba9dc6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:21:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] virtio/gpu: trap blobs, run on the storing vCPU's thread

A dxmt-context blob whose id has bit 63 set is left unmapped in the VM:
its map takes its guest range out of the host-visible window (backed
until a blob maps over it) and registers the range instead of an
hv_vm_map; its unmap drops it. A guest store there is an MMIO exit, and
the vCPU's thread hands the 8-byte value and the blob's context to the
handler the VM host sets with krun_set_trap_handler
(include/libkrun_trap.h), before the MMIO bus, reading the ranges
lock-free. A load there reads zeros.

The guest flushes a command ring by storing its blob id: the host runs
the ring on that vCPU, with no consumer thread spinning or parked.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
